    "heightBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSMway27715355/Q1568660 matches current main35184399804187. Six unscaled main/part/tower controls retain every raw tag and missing min_height. Main11m and northwest bell14m are current map heights; the retained main describes3building levels with no measured height. Both central square and round controls are tagged17m and share the modeled drum-top datum rather than being stacked as two17m solids. Low roofs,8.8m central apse,5.7m side apses, body/drum divisions, bell openings and dome/cross above17m are picture-led estimates; no surveyed dimensions claimed.",
    "scope": "Individual medium-fi Hagia Sophia in Thessaloniki: ochre west upper facade and exposed warm masonry lower/east walls, three west doors with a broad round central portal, four lower arched window fields and a narrow upper clerestory row. Square brick drum with large arched glazing, short round crown and low ribbed gray-green metal dome/cross. Low red tiled main roof, large polygonal eastern apse with smaller side apses, and northwest small bell tower/open paired arches and hip cap. Retained mapped plans and terrain-following footings. Separate unmapped courtyard gateway/retaining wall/fence, surrounding town/landscaping, exact carved reliefs/icons/text, interiors and certified walking excluded."
